# Line endings.
#
# Shell scripts and Dockerfiles are executed inside Linux containers. A
# CRLF checkout on Windows gives them "\r" at the end of the shebang, and
# the container fails with the memorable and unhelpful:
#
#     /bin/sh^M: bad interpreter: No such file or directory
#
# Forcing LF here means the file is correct in the image regardless of which
# machine committed it.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.dockerfile    text eol=lf
entrypoint.sh   text eol=lf

# Batch files are the mirror image: they run on Windows and want CRLF.
*.bat           text eol=crlf
